# F6: a bilinear Patch's "P" carries four vertex-class points (twelve
# floats); this supplies two. GMANParameterList sizes its destination from
# the declared class and used to copy that many floats from the supplied
# array regardless of its real length -- ASan a heap-buffer-overflow READ
# in GMANParameterList::copy_float before the clamp. gman is expected to
# warn, clamp, zero-fill and keep going.
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
AttributeBegin
	Patch "bilinear" "P" [-1 -1 0  1 -1 0]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
	Translate 2 0 0
	Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
